{
  "meta": {
    "description": "FEAT-2326609792 inc1 golden vectors — cross-language regression for the scale-ladder loader + log-linear interpolator. Consumed identically by internal/engine/traffic/scaleladder_test.go and webconsole/test/scaleLadder.test.ts.",
    "toleranceRule": "rung-exact queries (kind=exact) compare with tolerance 0 (exact float64 equality); interpolated queries (kind=interpolated) compare with a relative epsilon of 1e-12: |got-want| <= 1e-12 * max(1, |want|).",
    "roundCountRule": "roundCount(x) = floor(x + 0.5) for non-negative x — the ONE shared rounding rule for integer-valued fields (AC-7); Go's RoundCount and TypeScript's roundCount must agree byte-for-byte on expectedRoundedPeopleCount.",
    "mutantNote": "population=3000 sits between rungs 1000 and 5000 on the log scale but NOT on the linear scale (linear midpoint would be 3000, coincidentally equal here on the raw number, so the field VALUES are what red a linear-in-population mutant: a mutant that computes w=(p-p_i)/(p_{i+1}-p_i) instead of the log-linear formula produces different field values, caught by the exact expectedFields comparison)."
  },
